###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Training errors are stated only as bounds ('most of the predictions fall within +/-5 meV per f.u. for energy, +/-50 meV/A for force components and +/-3 kBar for stress'); phonons of reference phases, vortex textures, polymorph energies (Tables I-II) and switching barriers are property comparisons.
# - The paper calls the VASP models 'kernel-based GAPs implemented in VASP' trained with the Bayesian on-the-fly framework; they are mapped to the registry method VASP-MLFF.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/robredomagro2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.
